WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.980
Speaker 1: OK, this you really have to see
on Fox and Friends yesterday morning there,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.180
one of their three hosts, Brian Kilmeade,
was reduced to arguing with children about

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:15.179
Trump vs. Biden in a segment that if he was
able to feel shame, he should be completely

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:17.740
humiliated by his participation in this segment.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:24.470
An 11 year old kid pretty accurately makes
the case that he's feeling better about getting

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.960
back to school and about handling the pandemic.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.501
Now that Joe Biden is president and is dealing
with the coronavirus in a serious way, completely

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.620
reasonable position.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.320
It's an 11 year old kid.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.800
Kilmeade sort of seems to crack.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.350
He didn't like the kids comment, I guess,
and he sort of like responds rudely to the

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.350
kid.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.350
It's very weird.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.350
Take a look at this.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.660
Speaker 4: How close are you to getting back
in the room?

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.190
What do you miss most about not being in school?

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:55.140
Speaker 5: I miss most obviously seeing my
friends and all the after school activities

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.140
that I've done.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.809
And I think that we're very, very close to
getting back to school.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:07.299
And I think that on the way that our new president
is handling things is a very good way.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:12.130
And we would not have gone to this if it were
still the last president.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.480
Speaker 4: Really, that's hard to believe
because the last president was saying, I want

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.609
every kid back in school.

00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:23.479
So luckily for you, what is your hope knowing
the numbers are going down and the governor

00:01:23.479 --> 00:01:24.479
might be opening up?

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:29.869
Speaker 1: Did you notice that Kilmeade even
moved on to the next kid right away before

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:33.390
the eleven year old could refute kill Medes?

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.499
Completely flaccid counterpoint.

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:37.679
He doesn't want the kid to say another word.

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:41.240
Now, a source at Fox News told me after the
interview, Kilmeade referred to the kid as

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.749
a poopy head.

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:46.139
And that seems on brand with the way this
entire segment went.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.299
Who thought this was a good idea?

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:52.130
Who who conceives of this segment and thinks
it's a good idea.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:57.349
And if it wasn't Kilmeade and the segment
was put in front of him, why not react by

00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:02.049
saying, interesting, it's so great that you're
involved in following what's going on?

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:08.440
What can can Brian Kilmeade feel anything
but complete and total shame over this segment?

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.099
Or at least should he?

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:15.130
Who wants to bet that this kid's parents end
up getting threats as a result of the segment?

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.860
That's the serious thing.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.620
And unfortunately, it wouldn't be even remotely
surprising to me.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.030
And again, why even try to counter what an
eleven year old is saying?

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:32.370
If you strongly refute a kid, you're beating
an eleven year old in a debate.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.540
And of course, if the kid makes more sense
than you, which was actually the case here,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.120
you really look like a moron.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.340
And it's almost like that game show.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.349
Are you smarter than a fifth grader or a sixth
grader or whatever?

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.379
It's the Fox News edition of that game show.

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:47.390
And the hosts are losing badly.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.129
Like imagine feeling the urge to debate and
disprove rather than encourage a kid for their

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:55.400
involvement in what's going on in the world
around them.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.579
And this is how propaganda motivates people
to behave.

00:02:58.579 --> 00:03:00.440
Every differing opinion.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.159
It doesn't matter how minor.

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:07.230
It doesn't matter how nonthreatening the purveyor
of the opinion is.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.900
It is perceived as a threat that must be dealt
with immediately.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.050
You know, interesting.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.749
Thanks for sharing your opinion.

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:18.930
It's great to see kids involved in their country
taking an interest.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:19.930
Great.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:20.930
No, no.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.340
Instead, Kilmeade argues and then argues with
and then cuts off an eleven year old kid.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.319
Now, I'm being totally serious here.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:31.250
This is not I'm not joking about this.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:36.780
If you replaced Kilmeade with this eleven
year old on Fox and Friends, it would be a

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.340
way better and more interesting show.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.599
I might become a regular viewer of Fox and
Friends if this kid was mixing it up with

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:47.550
Steve Doocy and Ainsley Erhart instead of
Brian Kilmeade, that would make it a better

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.550
show.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:52.480
And I'm not kidding when I say the kid seems
better informed than most of the Fox News

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.480
audience.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.989
I have no doubt whatsoever about that.

00:03:54.989 --> 00:04:00.109
Now, for a moment, let's deal with the substance
of Brian Kilmeade rebuttal.

00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:01.109
Kilmeade is right.

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:05.489
Trump said, open every school and put every
kid back in school.

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:07.400
It was the middle of a pandemic.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:14.220
We had not nearly enough testing, no guidelines
about how to safely open schools absent vaccination.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.420
And we had no vaccines.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.470
We had no precautions.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:17.709
We had no preventative measures.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:19.750
Trump just said, open it all up.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:25.300
It's true, Trump said it, but it would have
been insanely dangerous to open schools when

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.500
and how Donald Trump said he wanted to do
it.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.710
And fortunately, it didn't happen.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.310
Now Joe Biden is doing it and it's being done
safely.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.220
And it's abundantly, abundantly clear who
got the right side of that argument.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.270
It wasn't Kilmeade.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:05:45.029
It was the eleven year old kid.

